body:
@coredevelopers, can you please look at this because its breaking my deploys because of this issue.

In BaseFileHelper::createDirectory() an error is thrown for:
-  mkdir <--> when a folder already exists

Although this is logical from a sequential perspective in BaseFileHelper::createDirectory(), it isnt logical in itself and errors apply in practice. Usecases:
- testserver: parallel testing 
- production: many requests & creating folders at the same time 

``` php
try {
            $result = mkdir($path, $mode);
            chmod($path, $mode);
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            throw new \yii\base\Exception("Failed to create directory '$path': " . $e->getMessage(), $e->getCode(), $e);
        }
```

>  But I still wonder if there are cases when you need that error or want custom handling for it.

Unlikely. The result method should look like following:

``` php
public static function createDirectory($path, $mode = 0775, $recursive = true)
    {
        if (is_dir($path)) {
            return true;
        }
        $parentDir = dirname($path);
        if ($recursive && !is_dir($parentDir)) {
            static::createDirectory($parentDir, $mode, true);
        }
        try {
            $result = mkdir($path, $mode);
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            if (!is_dir($path)) {
                throw new \yii\base\Exception("Failed to create directory '$path': " . $e->getMessage(), $e->getCode(), $e);
            } else {
                $result = true;
            }
        }
        try {
            chmod($path, $mode);
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            throw new \yii\base\Exception("Failed to change permissions for directory '$path': " . $e->getMessage(), $e->getCode(), $e);
        }

        return $result;
    }
```

The idea is: if there is a error while creating a directory and directory exists in result - it is not error at all.
